# No passwords here: each secret is a reference to a variable exported where the deploy runs,
# and the kit resolves it there (#19). Real deployments export them from the CI secret store.
# This file is committed on purpose, as the example a client repo copies — which is exactly why
# it must not hold a password.
#
# For dev-server, the simulated host, see "Deploying to dev-server" in README.md.
#
# The one literal: dev-server's registry has no authentication, so this is not a credential.
# A real project writes KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD, and the kit injects it.
KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=unused-by-a-local-registry
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=$POSTGRES_PASSWORD
APP_DB_PASSWORD=$APP_DB_PASSWORD
ConnectionStrings__Default=$APP_DATABASE_URL
